import{_ as o,o as e,c as i,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 236 | Realm and War: How the Symbiotic Faction Resolves Conflict in Non-Predatory Ways","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 236 | Realm and War: How the Symbiotic Faction Resolves Conflict in Non-Predatory Ways","no":236,"module":1,"tags":["Realm","War","Conflict Resolution","Non-Predation"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise","03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter","48-Judicial System and Adjudication Mechanism"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0236_模块1-境界与战争-共生派如何以非掠夺方式化解冲突.md","filePath":"en/0236_模块1-境界与战争-共生派如何以非掠夺方式化解冲突.md"}'),n={name:"en/0236_模块1-境界与战争-共生派如何以非掠夺方式化解冲突.md"};function r(s,t,l,c,d,h){return e(),i("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-236-realm-and-war-how-the-symbiotic-faction-resolves-conflict-in-non-predatory-ways" tabindex="-1">Entry 236 | Realm and War: How the Symbiotic Faction Resolves Conflict in Non-Predatory Ways <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-236-realm-and-war-how-the-symbiotic-faction-resolves-conflict-in-non-predatory-ways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 236 | Realm and War: How the Symbiotic Faction Resolves Conflict in Non-Predatory Ways&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 1 · In-Depth Realm Refinement | Baseline references: Documents 04, 03, 48</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-not-using-war-to-solve-war" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Not using war to solve war <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-not-using-war-to-solve-war" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Not using war to solve war&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In Heng Yuan Zhou (Wanling Hengmao Origin Cosmos)&#39;s cultivation civilization, war is not the preferred way to resolve conflict — in fact, after the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization was established, large-scale war has basically disappeared. But this does not mean no conflict: inter-race resource disputes, inter-plane law friction, residual predatory forces&#39; harassment — these conflicts still exist. The difference is: <strong>how does the Symbiotic Faction resolve these conflicts in non-predatory ways?</strong></p><p>The six top-level axioms in the relationship between realm and war — the anti-predation axiom directly negates war predation; the republican axiom of Myriad Races provides peaceful resolution frameworks; the collective ascension axiom guides conflict parties toward co-construction; the causal self-discipline axiom constrains conflict operations not to expand karma; the law-first axiom ensures conflict resolution mechanisms&#39; law definitions are stable; the universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>This entry analyzes the Symbiotic Faction&#39;s complete conflict resolution system.</p><h2 id="i-four-tier-conflict-resolution-mechanism" tabindex="-1">I. Four-Tier Conflict Resolution Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-four-tier-conflict-resolution-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Four-Tier Conflict Resolution Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Conflict Level</th><th>Resolution Method</th><th>Participants</th><th>Correspondence Realm</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Personal conflict</td><td>Mediation + arbitration</td><td>Community mediation committee</td><td>Transform - Law Origin</td></tr><tr><td>Racial conflict</td><td>Myriad Races Republican Assembly negotiation</td><td>Each race&#39;s representatives</td><td>Dao - Dao Integration</td></tr><tr><td>Plane conflict</td><td>Cross-plane coordination committee</td><td>Boundary-Breaking strong ones</td><td>Boundary-Breaking - World-Creation</td></tr><tr><td>Cosmic conflict</td><td>Origin Realm collective decision</td><td>Plane Transcendents</td><td>Origin Realm+</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="ii-why-the-symbiotic-faction-does-not-fight" tabindex="-1">II. Why the Symbiotic Faction Does Not Fight <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-the-symbiotic-faction-does-not-fight" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why the Symbiotic Faction Does Not Fight&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_2-1-war-is-a-zero-sum-game" tabindex="-1">2.1 War Is a Zero-Sum Game <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-1-war-is-a-zero-sum-game" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.1 War Is a Zero-Sum Game&quot;">​</a></h3><p>In predatory-faction systems, war is a means to acquire resources — win and you rob the loser&#39;s resources. But in the Symbiotic Faction&#39;s positive-sum system, war&#39;s cost far exceeds benefit: the cultivation environment war destroys takes centuries to recover; cultivators war kills are civilization&#39;s talent loss; war-triggered karma disturbance takes long-term repair.</p><p><strong>War&#39;s cost is always higher than negotiation&#39;s cost</strong> — this is the Symbiotic Faction&#39;s fundamental economic reason for not fighting.</p><h3 id="_2-2-war-cultivates-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">2.2 War Cultivates Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-2-war-cultivates-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.2 War Cultivates Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h3><p>War not only destroys matter, but also destroys people&#39;s hearts. A cultivator accustomed to &quot;win and grab resources&quot; finds it hard to accept symbiotic circulation ideals. From an education perspective, war is predatory thinking&#39;s breeding ground — the Symbiotic Faction rooting out war from the root is rooting out predatory thinking&#39;s revival from the root.</p><h3 id="_2-3-strong-ones-do-not-need-war-to-prove-power" tabindex="-1">2.3 Strong Ones Do Not Need War to Prove Power <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-3-strong-ones-do-not-need-war-to-prove-power" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.3 Strong Ones Do Not Need War to Prove Power&quot;">​</a></h3><p>In predatory-faction systems, strong ones display power and gain prestige through war. In the Symbiotic Faction system, strong ones&#39; prestige comes from contribution and responsibility — how much you do for Myriad Races determines how much prestige you have. No need to prove oneself through fighting.</p><h2 id="iii-the-conflict-resolution-toolbox" tabindex="-1">III. The Conflict Resolution Toolbox <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-the-conflict-resolution-toolbox" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. The Conflict Resolution Toolbox&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Although the Symbiotic Faction does not fight, this does not mean no &quot;strength&quot; — it&#39;s just that strength is used to resolve conflict not create it:</p><h3 id="_3-1-mediation-and-arbitration" tabindex="-1">3.1 Mediation and Arbitration <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-1-mediation-and-arbitration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.1 Mediation and Arbitration&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The community mediation committee is composed of Transform - Law Origin cultivators, responsible for personal and small-group conflicts. Mediation is based on the symbiotic constitution and cultivation ethics; a solution both sides can accept is the final solution.</p><h3 id="_3-2-resource-reallocation" tabindex="-1">3.2 Resource Reallocation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-2-resource-reallocation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.2 Resource Reallocation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>When conflict stems from resource struggle, the Joint Contracting mechanism starts resource reallocation — not &quot;loser gives resources to winner,&quot; but reallocation based on both sides&#39; actual contribution and needs.</p><h3 id="_3-3-knowledge-sharing-plans" tabindex="-1">3.3 Knowledge Sharing Plans <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-3-knowledge-sharing-plans" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.3 Knowledge Sharing Plans&quot;">​</a></h3><p>When conflict stems from knowledge monopoly, the Alaya Network mandates sharing — cultivation knowledge you hoard must be made public, letting both conflict parties cultivate with the same knowledge system.</p><h3 id="_3-4-cross-race-cooperation-projects" tabindex="-1">3.4 Cross-Race Cooperation Projects <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-4-cross-race-cooperation-projects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.4 Cross-Race Cooperation Projects&quot;">​</a></h3><p>When inter-racial conflict arises, the Myriad Races Republican Assembly starts cross-race cooperation projects — letting two races find common interest in cooperation, turning opposition into collaboration.</p><h3 id="_3-5-isolation-and-sanctions" tabindex="-1">3.5 Isolation and Sanctions <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-5-isolation-and-sanctions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.5 Isolation and Sanctions&quot;">​</a></h3><p>For residual predatory forces that refuse mediation and continuously harm symbiotic order, plane isolation and cultivation restrictions are applied. This &quot;don&#39;t fight but lock up&quot; method both protects symbiotic order and avoids war&#39;s karmic cost.</p><h2 id="iv-high-realm-strong-ones-role-in-conflict-resolution" tabindex="-1">IV. High-Realm Strong Ones&#39; Role in Conflict Resolution <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-high-realm-strong-ones-role-in-conflict-resolution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. High-Realm Strong Ones&#39; Role in Conflict Resolution&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Transform - Law Origin</strong>: community mediators, handling personal and small-group conflicts</li><li><strong>Dao - Dao Integration</strong>: racial conflict coordinators, participating in Myriad Races Republican Assembly negotiation</li><li><strong>Boundary-Breaking - World-Creation</strong>: plane conflict arbiters, cross-plane coordination</li><li><strong>Origin Realm</strong>: cosmic-level conflict&#39;s final adjudicator, but adjudication based on whole consensus not personal will</li></ul><p>High-realm strong ones&#39; role in conflict resolution is not &quot;beat the other side,&quot; but &quot;find a solution both sides can accept.&quot; This is far harder than fighting — fighting only needs power, reconciliation needs wisdom.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Universal infinite backstop</strong>: the universal equal infinite law establishes that every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing have a guarantee, strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose, predation naturally loses meaning</li><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: not fighting avoids war&#39;s enormous energy waste — the energy and talent war consumes, used for construction can create tenfold value</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: negating war predation from the root, conflict resolution all based on positive-sum game</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo systems&#39; conflict resolution method is fighting — the winner robs the loser; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s conflict resolution all based on negotiation and mediation</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: conflict resolution mechanisms are equally open to every Myriad Races group, no favoritism by race identity</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the conflict resolution toolbox expands with cosmos expansion, cross-cosmos conflict has corresponding coordination mechanisms</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The relationship between realm and war is not &quot;the stronger the better at fighting,&quot; but &quot;the stronger the less need to fight.&quot; In predatory-faction systems, war is part of cultivation — kill monsters to level up, rob resources, fight for hegemon; in the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, war is civilization&#39;s failure — if negotiation works, no fighting; if mediation works, no confrontation. The higher a cultivator reaches, the more they should become a peace promoter, not a war tool. This is the Symbiotic Faction&#39;s definition of &quot;strong one&quot;: not the strongest warrior, but the best mediator.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise</a> · <a href="./03-共生文明宪章.html">03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter</a> · <a href="./48-司法体系与裁决机制.html">48-Judicial System and Adjudication Mechanism</a></li></ul>',37)])])}const g=o(n,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
